---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Speaking & Workshops" description="Invite Dr. Ramesh Kayyam to speak on leadership, human-centered AI, organizational change, and the future of work.">
  <section class="speaking-hero"><div class="stage-lines" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="container hero-content"><p class="eyebrow">Speaking & Workshops</p><h1>Conversations that help people lead with clarity, courage, and care.</h1><p>Dr. Ramesh Kayyam brings a practical, human perspective to leadership, technology, change, and lifelong learning.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="/contact">Request an engagement</a><a class="button button--ghost" href="#why-leadership">Why this conversation matters</a></div></div></section>

  <section id="why-leadership" class="paper section why"><div class="container why-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Why leadership conversations matter</p><h2 class="section-title">The gap between a good leader and a bad leader is felt every day.</h2><div class="gold-rule"></div><p class="intro-text">Leadership development cannot be treated as an occasional event. It is a continuing responsibility—especially when work, technology, and expectations are changing quickly.</p></div><div class="why-copy"><p>Before the COVID-19 pandemic, many organizations regularly invested in leadership sessions and development for their management teams. In many workplaces, that focus lost momentum after the disruption. Employees now often speak openly about the distance between the leaders they need and the leadership they experience.</p><p>That distance affects trust, well-being, innovation, performance, and the willingness of people to bring their best ideas forward. It is why honest conversations with leadership experts, employees, and decision-makers are essential—not optional.</p></div></div></section>

  <section class="section stories"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">What people are telling us</p><h2 class="section-title">The cost of leadership without understanding.</h2><div class="story-grid"><article><span>01</span><h3>When expertise is ignored</h3><p>In one conversation with a corporate employee, the topic moved from work to stress, anxiety, and leadership. The employee described having to explain everyday processes repeatedly to a manager who still held the power to decide promotions and job security.</p><p class="takeaway">Leadership must be informed by the work people actually do.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>When AI becomes a command</h3><p>In another conversation, an employee described a manager who pushed for automation everywhere without understanding artificial intelligence, its outcomes, or the concerns of the people expected to implement it.</p><p class="takeaway">Technology succeeds when leaders listen before they demand change.</p></article></div><p class="disclaimer">These stories are shared anonymously and represent common workplace concerns, not specific organizations or individuals.</p></div></section>

  <section class="paper section topics"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Signature topics</p><h2 class="section-title">Conversations designed for the world people are working in now.</h2><div class="topic-list"><article><span>01</span><div><h3>Leadership in the AI Era</h3><p>Helping leaders meet technological change with confidence, purpose, and ethical clarity.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h3>Human-Centered Artificial Intelligence</h3><p>Balancing innovation with empathy, wisdom, responsibility, and the realities of work.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h3>Adaptive Leadership & Change</h3><p>Building the trust, communication, and resilience that help people move through uncertainty.</p></div></article><article><span>04</span><div><h3>The Future of Work</h3><p>Preparing organizations and individuals for changing roles, new tools, and meaningful opportunity.</p></div></article></div></div></section>

  <section class="section formats"><div class="container formats-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Built for your audience</p><h2 class="section-title">From an opening keynote to an ongoing learning experience.</h2><p class="section-copy">Each engagement can be shaped around your audience, organizational context, and the conversation you need to have now.</p></div><div class="format-list"><article><b>Keynotes</b><p>Thoughtful, energizing talks that open a meaningful conversation.</p></article><article><b>Workshops</b><p>Interactive sessions that turn leadership ideas into practical reflection and action.</p></article><article><b>Universities & Communities</b><p>Engaging discussions for students, educators, researchers, and lifelong learners.</p></article><article><b>Virtual Sessions</b><p>Focused conversations that bring people together across locations.</p></article></div></div></section>

  <section class="speaking-cta"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Start a conversation</p><h2>Bring a more human conversation about leadership to your community.</h2><a class="button" href="/contact">Connect with Dr. Ramesh</a></div></section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .speaking-hero{position:relative;overflow:hidden;min-height:700px;padding:11rem 0 6rem;background:radial-gradient(circle at 78% 20%,#604522 0,#211b13 44%,#0d0d0d 75%)}.hero-content{position:relative;z-index:2;max-width:980px}.hero-content h1{font-size:clamp(3.5rem,6.8vw,6.55rem);letter-spacing:-.07em;margin:.85rem 0 1.25rem}.hero-content>p:not(.eyebrow){max-width:655px;color:#d5cec1;font-size:1.12rem}.hero-actions{display:flex;gap:.8rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:2.1rem}.stage-lines{position:absolute;right:-12%;bottom:-43%;width:67%;height:98%;border:1px solid rgba(214,181,107,.17);transform:rotate(25deg);box-shadow:0 0 0 75px transparent,0 0 0 76px rgba(214,181,107,.1),0 0 0 151px transparent,0 0 0 152px rgba(214,181,107,.07)}
  .why-grid,.formats-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:7rem}.intro-text{max-width:480px;color:#59534a;font-size:1.02rem}.why-copy{font-size:1.07rem;color:#59544b}.why-copy p:first-child{margin-top:0}.why-copy p{margin-bottom:1.45rem}.stories{background:#111}.story-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;margin-top:3.5rem;border-top:1px solid rgba(214,181,107,.3);border-left:1px solid rgba(214,181,107,.3)}.story-grid article{padding:1.75rem;border-right:1px solid rgba(214,181,107,.3);border-bottom:1px solid rgba(214,181,107,.3)}.story-grid span,.topic-list span{color:var(--gold);font-size:.68rem;letter-spacing:.1em}.story-grid h3{font-size:1.85rem;margin:2.2rem 0 .75rem}.story-grid p{color:#c7bfb3;font-size:.97rem}.story-grid .takeaway{margin:2.3rem 0 0;color:var(--gold-light);font-family:'Playfair Display',Georgia,serif;font-size:1.23rem;line-height:1.35}.disclaimer{color:#aaa298;font-size:.75rem;margin:1.2rem 0 0}.topics{padding-bottom:6.8rem}.topic-list{margin-top:3.2rem;border-top:1px solid #d8d0c1}.topic-list article{display:grid;grid-template-columns:85px 1fr;gap:1rem;padding:1.5rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #d8d0c1}.topic-list h3{font-size:1.55rem;margin:0 0 .5rem}.topic-list p{margin:0;color:#5b554b;max-width:650px}.formats{background:linear-gradient(120deg,#142019,#111)}.formats-grid{align-items:start}.formats-grid .section-copy{margin-top:1.5rem}.format-list{border-top:1px solid rgba(214,181,107,.32)}.format-list article{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.2fr;gap:1rem;padding:1.2rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(214,181,107,.32)}.format-list b{font-family:'Playfair Display',Georgia,serif;font-size:1.3rem}.format-list p{color:#c5bdb1;font-size:.91rem;margin:0}.speaking-cta{text-align:center;padding:6.3rem 1rem;background:var(--gold);color:var(--ink)}.speaking-cta h2{font-size:clamp(2.55rem,5.5vw,4.6rem);max-width:900px;margin:.7rem auto 1.75rem}.speaking-cta .eyebrow{color:#5b461b}.speaking-cta .button{background:#111;color:var(--ivory);border-color:#111}@media(max-width:750px){.speaking-hero{padding-top:9rem;min-height:640px}.why-grid,.formats-grid,.story-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:2.5rem}.story-grid{margin-top:2.5rem}.topic-list article{grid-template-columns:55px 1fr}}@media(max-width:520px){.hero-content h1{font-size:3.35rem}.format-list article{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:.3rem}}
</style>
